WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:05.506
What defines you?

00:00:05.964 --> 00:00:07.716
There’s nothing I wouldn’t do
for my daughter.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.096
I've loved Laura Dave's book,

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.516
The Last Thing He Told Me,
from the get-go.

00:00:15.891 --> 00:00:19.102
There's an engine under it that just
makes you want to keep reading.

00:00:19.186 --> 00:00:21.438
The show has that same kind of energy.

00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:23.774
The series is really asking the question,

00:00:24.608 --> 00:00:26.860
"Can we ever really know
the person we love?"

00:00:26.944 --> 00:00:29.655
And what we're willing to do
for our children.

00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:32.574
Hey, it’s Owen.
Leave a message.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.453
The Last Thing He Told Me
is, above all else, a love story.

00:00:36.537 --> 00:00:39.122
Hannah Hall loves Owen Michaels.

00:00:39.206 --> 00:00:41.166
Hannah fell in love later in life.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.962
She feels like there's a oneness
that she has with her husband.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.214
They've just begun their life together.

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:50.217
The big challenge for the relationship
is that he has a teenage daughter.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:50.926
I’ll wait out front.

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:54.388
And her relationship with Hannah
is as bad as you can get,

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.850
when suddenly one day
Owen doesn't come home.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.269
Mr. Michaels asked me
to give this to you.

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:06.024
I just spoke to my source
at the U.S. Attorney's office, Hann.

00:01:06.108 --> 00:01:07.776
Owen’s a material witness.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.028
They'll likely make him
a subject of the investigation.

00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:11.572
Where is he, Hannah?

00:01:11.655 --> 00:01:12.656
I don't know.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:16.743
Owen’s disappearance sets in motion
these two women,

00:01:17.202 --> 00:01:18.704
who are virtual strangers,

00:01:18.787 --> 00:01:20.914
trying to figure out
what happened to the person

00:01:20.998 --> 00:01:22.875
they both love more
than anyone in the world.

00:01:22.958 --> 00:01:24.543
You're not going to school tomorrow.

00:01:24.626 --> 00:01:25.252
I’m not?

00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:26.628
I have a new plan.

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:30.966
She very, very quickly has to learn
what it means to care for this daughter.

00:01:31.884 --> 00:01:36.889
Throughout the show, we get to see
Bailey understanding how to have a mother

00:01:36.972 --> 00:01:39.224
and Hannah understanding how to be one.

00:01:39.308 --> 00:01:40.642
He said he'd always be there.

00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:44.855
I don't know what's happening here,
but I do know your dad loves you.

00:01:45.898 --> 00:01:46.815
D mark.

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:48.734
And, action!

00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:54.531
The Last Thing He Told Me, as I read it,
you could see it play out in front of you.

00:01:54.615 --> 00:01:57.201
And I've loved being part of
this thrilling mystery.

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:01.997
The role of Hannah is that balance
between tough and vulnerable,

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.750
and Jen Garner, she's just extraordinary.

00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:08.837
She has been able to really tap into
Hannah's deep strength.

00:02:08.921 --> 00:02:12.883
Her trust in who Owen is as a person
is what keeps driving them

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:15.844
to solve this mystery
and trust her instincts

00:02:15.928 --> 00:02:18.305
that there's something more to the story.

00:02:18.388 --> 00:02:21.975
I may not know why your father did
what he did, but I know who he is.

00:02:22.059 --> 00:02:24.311
Watching Jen and Angourie together,

00:02:24.394 --> 00:02:27.272
the extraordinary talent
that they have as actresses,

00:02:27.356 --> 00:02:28.440
it's just been such a gift.

00:02:28.524 --> 00:02:31.443
And then you have Nikolaj.
He is incredible.

00:02:31.527 --> 00:02:33.987
Owen Michaels is not who you think he is.

00:02:34.655 --> 00:02:37.407
Why are you making him sound like
some sort of criminal mastermind?

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:42.746
You just get such a range of colors,
and you get the hints of this darker past.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.790
Even in his charm.

00:02:44.873 --> 00:02:46.583
He lied to me about everything.

00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:48.293
I want to know the truth!

00:02:49.044 --> 00:02:50.128
I'm telling you, we’ll find it.

00:02:51.463 --> 00:02:56.426
The tension between the mystery
and the relationships is really unique.

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:59.680
You feel like, "Oh, this is a mystery.
Oh, this is a thriller."

00:02:59.763 --> 00:03:03.392
But really, it's a story about parenting
and about motherhood.

00:03:03.475 --> 00:03:05.519
Together, they have to find the truth,

00:03:05.602 --> 00:03:07.437
and the mystery is incredible
as it unfolds.

00:03:08.856 --> 00:03:10.023
You're following these characters

00:03:10.107 --> 00:03:13.819
in a very intense
emotional point in their lives,

00:03:13.902 --> 00:03:16.530
and it makes for a great dramatic show

00:03:16.613 --> 00:03:19.032
that will keep audiences
on the edge of their seat.

00:03:19.533 --> 00:03:21.952
You said that people
don't run for no reason.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:23.787
Now the FBI is threatening me.

00:03:26.081 --> 00:03:28.333
Whatever this is, you want no part of it.

